-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 5, §5.1 יחידת עבודה
-- The work unit of a middle-school teacher, and the rules that follow one
-- who moves to teach grades 1-6.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `5.1 יחידת עבודה`

§§ `5.1.1`

@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_1__hc_2__para_1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly teaching hours in a middle-school work unit` IS 24

@desc The share of a full middle-school position that a number of weekly teaching hours makes.
GIVEN `weekly teaching hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `middle-school position fraction` `weekly teaching hours` IS
    `weekly teaching hours` DIVIDED BY `weekly teaching hours in a middle-school work unit`

§§ `5.1.2`

DECLARE `school level of the rules` IS ONE OF
    `the rules of middle-school teachers`
    `the rules that apply to primary-school teachers (see section 3.1)`

@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_1__hc_2__para_2
@desc Which rules govern a teaching employee: one moved from a middle school to teach grades 1-6 is under the same rules as primary-school teachers (see section 3.1, encoded there).
GIVEN `moved from the middle school to teach grades 1-6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `school level of the rules`
DECIDE `the rules that apply` `moved from the middle school to teach grades 1-6` IS
    IF `moved from the middle school to teach grades 1-6`
    THEN `the rules that apply to primary-school teachers (see section 3.1)`
    ELSE `the rules of middle-school teachers`

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_1__hc_3__para_1 Source (אסמכתא): the government–teachers' union agreement, a Director-General's circular and a 1977 memorandum.
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_1__hc_3__para_2 Source (אסמכתא): a decision of the supreme parity committee.

#ASSERT `middle-school position fraction` 18 EQUALS 0.75
#ASSERT `the rules that apply` TRUE EQUALS `the rules that apply to primary-school teachers (see section 3.1)`

§§ `Property checks`

-- 5.1.1 over every load of 0 to 24 weekly hours: the fraction is 0 to 1,
-- rises with every hour, and a full work unit is a whole position.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD
                    `middle-school position fraction` h AT LEAST 0
                AND `middle-school position fraction` h AT MOST 1
                AND `middle-school position fraction` (h PLUS 1) GREATER THAN `middle-school position fraction` h)
            (range 0 24)
#ASSERT `middle-school position fraction` 24 EQUALS 1

-- 5.1.2 over both cases: exactly one set of rules applies, and the two
-- cases get different ones.
#ASSERT NOT (`the rules that apply` TRUE EQUALS `the rules that apply` FALSE)
